1
00:00:07,450 --> 00:00:10,733
Okay chat, we're live. Look at this guy.

2
00:00:11,053 --> 00:00:17,211
Three years dead and he still mows his lawn. That's more than my dad ever did.

3
00:00:18,331 --> 00:00:19,575
Phone down, Vo.

4
00:00:21,331 --> 00:00:26,699
Moss, we're at four hundred viewers. The algorithm loves commuters.

5
00:00:27,819 --> 00:00:29,635
The algorithm doesn't bleed.

6
00:00:33,819 --> 00:00:36,299
Sorry, buddy. Lawn looks great.

7
00:00:44,269 --> 00:00:47,687
Good morning, Team Eleven! Happy Double Bonus Saturday!

8
00:00:48,007 --> 00:00:53,981
Every confirmed Rotter is worth twice the points this weekend. Remember: a clean zone is a happy zone!

9
00:00:55,101 --> 00:00:58,759
I love her. She sounds like a yogurt commercial.

10
00:00:59,879 --> 00:01:03,597
She sounds like a hostage negotiator. For the kidnapper.

11
00:01:04,717 --> 00:01:10,288
Today's target: Pinecrest Mall. Estimated two hundred commuters. Quota: one-eighty.

12
00:01:10,608 --> 00:01:13,861
Fall below quota and, well... you know the policy!

13
00:01:14,981 --> 00:01:16,157
What's the policy?

14
00:01:17,981 --> 00:01:19,888
We don't talk about Team Nine.

15
00:01:25,831 --> 00:01:31,178
Oh my God. They're waiting in line. Chat, they're still waiting in line.

16
00:01:32,298 --> 00:01:36,597
Some things survive the apocalypse. Brand loyalty's one of them.

17
00:01:37,717 --> 00:01:41,605
I waited forty minutes there once. For the fish sandwich.

18
00:01:41,925 --> 00:01:42,977
Was it worth it?

19
00:01:43,297 --> 00:01:44,083
...No.

20
00:01:50,203 --> 00:01:57,064
Okay, that one had braces. Who gets braces in the apocalypse? That's optimism!

21
00:02:00,185 --> 00:02:03,959
My phone! Not the phone! I have sponsors!

22
00:02:09,429 --> 00:02:11,880
Bruno... you want me to...

23
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:15,292
No. I've got this one.

24
00:02:24,412 --> 00:02:25,673
He wanted a bike.

25
00:02:25,993 --> 00:02:26,503
Yeah.

26
00:02:32,262 --> 00:02:38,465
Halcyon, Team Eleven. We have survivors. Four civilians. Requesting evac.

27
00:02:39,585 --> 00:02:44,758
Ooh. That's awkward. Survivors aren't really in this quarter's KPIs, Marcus.

28
00:02:45,878 --> 00:02:46,859
They're people.

29
00:02:48,878 --> 00:02:52,807
And people are wonderful! But evacuation is a separate contract.

30
00:02:53,127 --> 00:02:58,420
Please complete your quota and seal the east doors on your way out. Great energy today, team!

31
00:02:59,540 --> 00:03:03,383
Did she just tell us to lock a family in a zombie mall?

32
00:03:04,503 --> 00:03:06,493
She said it with a smile, though.

33
00:03:10,613 --> 00:03:13,514
Vo. How many people are watching your stream?

34
00:03:13,834 --> 00:03:17,844
With the cracked screen? Like... eleven thousand.

35
00:03:18,164 --> 00:03:20,122
Good. Keep it on them.

36
00:03:27,592 --> 00:03:31,263
Excuse me. Pardon. Excuse me.

37
00:03:42,233 --> 00:03:46,292
One point two million. That's the most I've ever had.

38
00:03:47,412 --> 00:03:48,518
How's it feel?

39
00:03:48,838 --> 00:03:50,530
Like I want to throw up.

40
00:03:50,850 --> 00:03:52,362
Welcome to the job.

41
00:03:53,482 --> 00:04:00,460
Marcus. That stream was... unfortunate. Your team has been reassigned. Tomorrow, Sector Four.

42
00:04:01,580 --> 00:04:04,076
Sector Four was cleared last year.

43
00:04:05,196 --> 00:04:07,826
Not anymore! Sleep well, Team Eleven!

